# BUG-229: TUI apps SEGFAULTED at startup because the selfhost emit declared
# `var _tui_env: *std.process.Environ.Map = undefined;` and NEVER ASSIGNED IT, then
# passed it to zz.Terminal.init — a memory fault at 0xffffffffffffffff.
#
# It was the FOURTH GUI crash to sit underneath a full set of green gates, and it went
# unpinned because "GUI bug" reads as "needs a human with a terminal". Most of it does.
# THIS part does not: the assignment either appears in the emitted Zig or it does not,
# which is a STATIC fact about text, checkable in about a second with no build, no
# terminal and no display.
#
# Registered with smoke_gui_emit_contains, asserting `_tui_env = ` appears in the emit.
# That is narrower than tools/gui_scaffold_check.sh (which builds a real app and checks
# every `= undefined` global, and remains the better tool) but unlike that one it is
# CHEAP enough to gate, so BUG-229 stops being a fixed bug with nothing watching it.
#
# What this does NOT cover, stated so it is not mistaken for GUI coverage: rendering,
# input, layout, resize, colours. Those still need Sean running the thing.
struct Model
    var n: int

def view(g: Gui, m: Model)
    g.text("bug229")

def main()
    Gui.run(Model(n: 0), def(g: Gui, m: Model) = view(g, m))
